00:27:27.370 --> 00:27:30.250
But that's about the extent of my basketball experience.
但这就是我篮球经验的全部了。

615
00:27:30.250 --> 00:27:31.250
And she goes, okay.
她说，好吧。

616
00:27:31.830 --> 00:27:32.530
Okay, great.
好吧，太棒了。

617
00:27:32.730 --> 00:27:37.970
I am shocked learning this information because we just re-watched the basketball episode,
听到这个消息我太震惊了，因为我们刚重温了那集篮球赛，

618
00:27:37.970 --> 00:27:41.490
and I think you play very well.
我觉得你打得很好。

619
00:27:41.790 --> 00:27:43.190
I would never know.
我完全看不出来。

620
00:27:43.350 --> 00:27:44.530
You said you don't dribble.
你说你不会运球。

621
00:27:44.530 --> 00:27:47.490
I'm like, I have no memory of you being a bad dripper.
我完全不记得你运球很烂。

622
00:27:47.490 --> 00:27:50.090
But if you look close, I never dribbled the ball down the court.
但如果你仔细看，我从来没有运球跑过全场。

623
00:27:50.190 --> 00:27:50.770
Is that right?
是这样吗？

624
00:27:50.870 --> 00:27:51.070
Nope.
没错。

625
00:27:51.350 --> 00:27:51.550
Never.
从来没有。

626
00:27:51.830 --> 00:27:52.110
Never.
从来没有。

627
00:27:52.350 --> 00:27:54.430
But you're really good at guarding Dwight.
但你防守德怀特真的很厉害。

628
00:27:54.570 --> 00:27:55.710
You held your own.
你表现得很稳。

629
00:27:55.710 --> 00:27:56.750
I knew how to guard.
我知道怎么防守。

630
00:27:56.990 --> 00:27:58.030
I knew how to guard.
我知道怎么防守。

631
00:27:58.290 --> 00:28:00.170
And I knew that much I knew.
这一点我还是知道的。

632
00:28:00.370 --> 00:28:08.030
And then when I think I found out I had booked it, and I went running to Target, and I ran,
后来我发现我接到了那个角色，我就跑去塔吉特百货，跑着，

633
00:28:08.030 --> 00:28:12.790
and I bought a basketball, and I came home, I told my husband, you need to teach me how
买了个篮球，回到家，我跟我丈夫说，你现在得教我怎么

634
00:28:12.790 --> 00:28:14.110
to dribble a basketball now.
运球。

635
00:28:14.470 --> 00:28:15.570
And he was like, what?
他当时就说，什么？

636
00:28:15.690 --> 00:28:17.150
And I said, you don't understand.
我说，你不明白。

637
00:28:17.450 --> 00:28:21.410
I just booked a show, and I need to learn how to play basketball.
我刚接了个戏，我得学会怎么打篮球。

638
00:28:21.630 --> 00:28:26.830
And he was like, honey, I can't teach you how to play basketball in, like, one weekend.
他说，亲爱的，我没法在一个周末内教会你打篮球。

639
00:28:26.830 --> 00:28:28.950
And I said, try, please, anything.
我说，试试吧，求你了，什么都行。

640
00:28:29.850 --> 00:28:33.290
So was that your weekend, you and your husband, like, trying to play basketball?
所以那个周末你们俩就在那儿试着打篮球？

641
00:28:33.510 --> 00:28:35.410
It was, like, cramming to try and play basketball.
没错，就像是临时抱佛脚，拼命想学会打篮球。

642
00:28:35.930 --> 00:28:38.510
And I sucked at it so badly.
我打得简直烂透了。

643
00:28:39.690 --> 00:28:41.590
And my husband is 6'5".
我丈夫有六英尺五英寸高。

644
00:28:42.030 --> 00:28:47.190
So it was like, he really was, like, blocking and doing all this stuff.
所以他真的就在那儿盖帽，做各种动作。

645
00:28:47.190 --> 00:28:48.410
And he was like, try and go around me.
他说，试着绕过我。

646
00:28:48.470 --> 00:28:49.490
And I was like, I can't.
我说，我做不到。

647
00:28:49.590 --> 00:28:50.310
You're too tall.
你太高了。

648
00:28:50.730 --> 00:28:52.670
And so I did my beSt.
所以我尽力了。

649
00:28:52.670 --> 00:28:53.510
I did my beSt.
我真的尽力了。

650
00:28:53.510 --> 00:28:55.490
And I practiced all weekend long.
我整个周末都在练习。

651
00:28:56.830 --> 00:28:57.690
Got to set.
得去片场了。

652
00:28:57.990 --> 00:29:02.930
It was funny, because the first day on set, I had to go through these massive wardrobe
挺有意思的，因为在片场的第一天，我试了好多套戏服，

653
00:29:02.930 --> 00:29:06.670
changes, because Greg was like, no, that's too frilly.
因为格雷格总说，不行，那件太花哨了。

654
00:29:06.770 --> 00:29:07.830
That's too frou-frou-y.
那件太繁琐了。

655
00:29:07.890 --> 00:29:09.150
We need to find something else.
我们得换一件。

656
00:29:09.170 --> 00:29:15.130
And they finally gave me the cutoff t-shirt with whatever number it was, a number 38 on it.
最后他们给了我一件剪短的T恤，上面印着个数字，好像是38号。

657
00:29:16.810 --> 00:29:17.790
Wait, what is that?
等等，那是什么？

658
00:29:17.850 --> 00:29:18.770
Is that a picture of you from set?
那是你在片场的照片吗？

659
00:29:18.770 --> 00:29:22.850
I made a postcard, because I was so excited about the show.
我做了一张明信片，因为我当时对这部剧太兴奋了。

660
00:29:22.970 --> 00:29:25.190
So I made a postcard to mail out.
所以我做了一张明信片寄出去。

661
00:29:25.190 --> 00:29:28.730
Because back in those days, you actually mailed out postcards as an announcement.
因为在那个年代，你确实会寄明信片来做宣传。

662
00:29:29.110 --> 00:29:29.310
Yeah.
没错。

663
00:29:29.590 --> 00:29:32.570
I did this when I did theater in L.A.
我以前在洛杉矶演舞台剧时也这么干过。

664
00:29:32.570 --> 00:29:32.870
Yeah.
是啊。

665
00:29:33.110 --> 00:29:35.650
You would put, like, a picture of yourself.
你会放上一张自己的照片。

666
00:29:35.650 --> 00:29:37.210
And there was, like, we had a quote.
上面还会印上一句评价。

667
00:29:37.350 --> 00:29:38.090
We were, like, L.A.
比如我们当时被《洛杉矶周刊》

668
00:29:38.190 --> 00:29:39.510
Weekly pick of the week.
评为“本周精选”。

669
00:29:39.770 --> 00:29:39.850
Right.
对。

670
00:29:40.010 --> 00:29:44.810
And then you would make a postcard, and you would mail that to all the casting directors in town.
然后你就会印好明信片，寄给城里所有的选角导演。

671
00:29:44.850 --> 00:29:46.790
When they had offices, right?
那时候他们还有办公室，对吧？

672
00:29:47.070 --> 00:29:49.490
I did the same thing backstage weSt.
我在“后台西部”也做过同样的事。

673
00:29:49.490 --> 00:29:49.930
Right?
是吧？

674
00:29:50.370 --> 00:29:56.050
And it was, so I, it was funny, because they couldn't find the right outfit for me, and
挺逗的，因为他们一开始找不到适合我的戏服，

675
00:29:56.050 --> 00:29:57.070
eventually they did.
后来终于找到了。

676
00:29:58.670 --> 00:30:01.250
And so we did that, and then.
我们就那样拍了，然后。

677
00:30:01.550 --> 00:30:03.230
This postcard is amazing.
这张明信片太棒了。

678
00:30:03.510 --> 00:30:05.070
It was, that was the best shot.
那是拍得最好的一张。

679
00:30:05.270 --> 00:30:06.830
I don't even remember who took that.
我都不记得是谁拍的了。

680
00:30:07.010 --> 00:30:10.990
What's so great about this picture, and I'll put it in our Insta stories, you guys, it's
这张照片最棒的地方在于——各位，我会把它发到我们的Instagram快拍里——

681
00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:12.130
Carly as Madge.
那是饰演玛奇的卡莉。

682
00:30:12.130 --> 00:30:19.150
You're dripping with sweat, and you look like you've just played a lot of basketball.
你满头大汗，看起来就像刚打完一场激烈的篮球赛。

683
00:30:19.350 --> 00:30:20.830
You have a really miserable expression.
你的表情看起来非常痛苦。

684
00:30:20.930 --> 00:30:22.850
It's the date and time of the episode.
上面还写着剧集的日期和时间。

685
00:30:23.030 --> 00:30:23.910
This is fantastic.
这太赞了。

686
00:30:24.310 --> 00:30:25.770
It was so much fun.
当时真的特别开心。

687
00:30:25.930 --> 00:30:30.670
I remember, because I went into hair and makeup, and I think, I know you were there, and Katie
我记得当时我去了化妆间，我想，我知道你在那儿，凯蒂

688
00:30:30.670 --> 00:30:31.110
was there.
也在那儿。

689
00:30:31.190 --> 00:30:32.830
One of you was there, and Katie was there.
你们其中一个在那儿，凯蒂也在那儿。

690
00:30:33.030 --> 00:30:35.970
And somebody looked up at me and said, don't expect much.
有人抬头看着我说：“别抱太大期望。”

691
00:30:36.130 --> 00:30:37.010
And I was like, what?
我当时就想，什么？

692
00:30:37.250 --> 00:30:37.850
Oh, no.
噢，不。

693
00:30:38.050 --> 00:30:39.670
Phyllis and Katie were in there.
菲利斯和凯蒂当时都在那儿。

694
00:30:39.810 --> 00:30:41.430
And they were like, don't expect much.
她们说：“别抱太大期望。”

695
00:30:41.430 --> 00:30:42.650
It's not that kind of show.
这不是那种类型的剧。

696
00:30:42.790 --> 00:30:43.910
And I was like, what do you mean?
我问：“你什么意思？”

697
00:30:44.010 --> 00:30:46.050
And it was like, there's no, there's no makeup.
她们说：“这里没有，这里根本不用化妆。”

698
00:30:46.370 --> 00:30:47.470
There's, there's like nada.
什么都没有，完全没有。

699
00:30:47.770 --> 00:30:50.090
And I was like, I'm okay, fine.
我说：“行吧，没问题。”

700
00:30:50.270 --> 00:30:51.570
I don't, this is me.
我不在乎，这就是我。

701
00:30:51.730 --> 00:30:52.510
I don't wear much.
我穿得不多。

702
00:30:52.610 --> 00:30:52.930
And they were like.
他们当时就说。

703
00:30:52.930 --> 00:30:55.590
I mean, Carly, you and I have the same hairstyle in this episode.
我是说，卡莉，这一集里你和我的发型一模一样。

704
00:30:55.930 --> 00:30:56.030
I know.
我知道。

705
00:30:56.170 --> 00:30:56.850
I know.
我知道。

706
00:30:56.990 --> 00:30:58.150
They put it in a braid.
他们把头发编成了辫子。

707
00:30:58.430 --> 00:31:00.090
We both just have a French braid and called it a day.
我们俩都只是扎了个法式辫子就完事了。

708
00:31:00.130 --> 00:31:01.170
Yeah, that was it.
是啊，就是这样。

709
00:31:01.170 --> 00:31:06.670
And I had the bangs back then, and, and they just kept getting sweatier and sweatier.
那时候我还有刘海，而且刘海变得越来越湿。

710
00:31:06.810 --> 00:31:10.550
And there was like, nobody cared about anything.
当时好像根本没人关心什么。

711
00:31:10.550 --> 00:31:16.030
The only mistake I made was, I think in the warehouse scene, I made the mistake of climbing
我唯一犯的错是，我想是在仓库那场戏里，我犯了个错，去爬了

712
00:31:16.030 --> 00:31:17.770
the rolling stairs.
那个移动梯子。

713
00:31:18.150 --> 00:31:18.770
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

714
00:31:18.950 --> 00:31:19.870
In the first scene.
在第一场戏里。

715
00:31:20.670 --> 00:31:23.330
And I think I had to do that 50 times.
我想我大概爬了50次。

716
00:31:23.890 --> 00:31:26.090
Oh, because they liked it and it had to match.
哦，因为他们喜欢那个镜头，而且得连戏。

717
00:31:26.530 --> 00:31:29.310
It was like taking, it was like doing a stair master.
那感觉就像是在用踏步机锻炼一样。

718
00:31:29.590 --> 00:31:31.790
So was that on your first day of shooting?
那是你拍摄的第一天吗？

719
00:31:31.790 --> 00:31:35.870
And then you had to come back with the sore legs and play basketball.
然后你还得拖着酸痛的双腿回来打篮球。

720
00:31:37.090 --> 00:31:38.410
And Leslie's trailer.
还有莱斯利的拖车。

721
00:31:38.770 --> 00:31:42.430
You know how we all had those honey wagons the very first episode?
你还记得第一集我们都有那种移动化妆车吗？

722
00:31:42.490 --> 00:31:42.650
Yeah, yeah.
记得，记得。

723
00:31:42.770 --> 00:31:44.410
And you decorated them for Halloween.
你还为了万圣节装饰了它们。

724
00:31:44.410 --> 00:31:45.450
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

725
00:31:45.650 --> 00:31:46.650
Kate and I, yes.
我和凯特，没错。

726
00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:47.970
We just talked about that.
我们刚聊到这个。

727
00:31:48.090 --> 00:31:49.950
We went to the 99 cent store and decorated everything.
我们去了99美分商店，把所有东西都装饰了一番。

728
00:31:49.950 --> 00:31:50.890
It was the cutest thing.
那真是太可爱了。

729
00:31:50.930 --> 00:31:53.810
Everybody had little booze and ghosts and everything.
每个人都有小酒瓶、鬼怪之类的装饰。

730
00:31:54.310 --> 00:31:58.710
But Leslie's trailer was here and then Brian and then me or whatever.
但莱斯利的拖车在那边，然后是布莱恩，再然后是我之类的。

731
00:31:58.910 --> 00:32:04.690
And I remember Leslie was sitting on his stairs and Brian was sitting on his.
我记得莱斯利坐在他的台阶上，布莱恩坐在他的台阶上。

732
00:32:04.870 --> 00:32:08.810
And I tried to get up into my trailer and I was like, ow.
我试着爬上我的拖车，然后我就说，哎哟。

733
00:32:09.030 --> 00:32:12.090
And Leslie looked at me and he goes, Arnica, Arnica.
莱斯利看着我说，山金车，山金车。

734
00:32:12.370 --> 00:32:12.970
And I was like, what?
我问，什么？

735
00:32:13.050 --> 00:32:15.970
And he goes, go get yourself some Arnica gel.
他说，去给自己买点山金车凝胶。

736
00:32:16.130 --> 00:32:17.070
It's the only thing.
那是唯一管用的东西。

737
00:32:17.230 --> 00:32:18.410
That and a hot bath.
再加上泡个热水澡。

738
00:32:18.610 --> 00:32:19.610
And I was like, okay.
我就说，好吧。

739
00:32:20.090 --> 00:32:22.010
That is so Leslie, isn't it?
这太像莱斯利的风格了，不是吗？

740
00:32:22.050 --> 00:32:22.890
A hot bath.
泡个热水澡。

741
00:32:22.890 --> 00:32:24.090
Yeah, I love it.
是啊，我喜欢。

742
00:32:24.090 --> 00:32:26.010
So many times you told us to take a hot bath.
你告诉过我们好多次要泡热水澡。

743
00:32:26.210 --> 00:32:29.670
My legs hurt so bad after the third day and we were filming.
第三天拍摄后我的腿疼得厉害。

744
00:32:29.890 --> 00:32:33.610
And all I kept doing was running up and down the court, up and down.
我一直在球场上跑来跑去，跑个不停。

745
00:32:33.790 --> 00:32:35.230
And we were on a concrete floor.
而且我们是在水泥地上拍的。

746
00:32:35.450 --> 00:32:35.710
Yeah.
是啊。

747
00:32:36.670 --> 00:32:38.650
And my legs hurt so bad.
我的腿疼得要命。

748
00:32:38.650 --> 00:32:41.790
It was like the third day and I was like, I couldn't walk anymore.
那是第三天，我感觉自己已经走不动了。

749
00:32:42.230 --> 00:32:44.330
Well, you know, we had the opposite problem.
嗯，你知道，我们遇到了相反的问题。

750
00:32:44.530 --> 00:32:45.410
You were sitting.
你一直在坐着。

751
00:32:45.770 --> 00:32:49.570
We sat on that metal bench with no cushion for three days.
我们坐在那张没有垫子的金属长椅上坐了三天。

752
00:32:49.570 --> 00:32:52.570
And my butt and legs kept falling asleep.
我的屁股和腿一直发麻。

753
00:32:53.230 --> 00:32:58.430
Or that thing that happens where like I also couldn't walk because I was like stiff from
或者那种情况，就是我也没法走路了，因为我整个人都僵住了，

754
00:32:58.430 --> 00:33:01.330
like sitting in the same position for hours and hours.
因为连续好几个小时都保持同一个姿势坐着。

755
00:33:01.610 --> 00:33:02.350
That's wow.
哇，那真是。

756
00:33:02.730 --> 00:33:04.910
Also, I mean, whatever, overshare.
而且，我是说，算了，说得太多了。

757
00:33:05.030 --> 00:33:08.030
But that bench had these long grooved lines in it.
但那张长椅上有那种长长的凹槽纹路。

758
00:33:08.210 --> 00:33:08.590
Yes.
没错。

759
00:33:08.590 --> 00:33:13.430
And when you went, when I went home and I changed clothes, I had like waffle balls.
当我回家换衣服的时候，我的皮肤上全是那种华夫饼格子的印子。

760
00:33:13.450 --> 00:33:13.790
Oh, no.
噢，天哪。

761
00:33:14.730 --> 00:33:18.890
But this is a really great tip for any aspiring actor out there.
但这对于任何有志于演戏的人来说，真的是一个很好的建议。

762
00:33:19.150 --> 00:33:24.190
Whatever you do in the background on the first take, you will be doing over and over and over
无论你在第一遍拍摄时在背景里做了什么动作，你之后都得一遍又一遍地

763
00:33:24.190 --> 00:33:24.490
again.
重复做。

764
00:33:24.490 --> 00:33:32.030
One of my friends had told me like a long time ago, never, ever, ever pick a tough job
很久以前我的一位朋友曾告诉我，千万、千万、千万别选那种辛苦的活儿

765
00:33:32.030 --> 00:33:32.530
to do.
来做。

766
00:33:32.890 --> 00:33:38.390
Like because on one, I think of one commercial shoot, he made the mistake of choosing a jackhammer.
因为有一次，我想是在拍某个广告时，他犯了个错，选了用手提钻。

767
00:33:38.630 --> 00:33:39.170
Oh, no.
噢，不。

768
00:33:39.170 --> 00:33:41.250
I was like, really sorry he ever did that.
我当时就觉得，真为他选了那个感到难过。

769
00:33:41.550 --> 00:33:46.210
And I'll never forget that because afterwards I was like, why did I choose to go up and down
我永远忘不了那次，因为事后我在想，我为什么要选上下

770
00:33:46.210 --> 00:33:46.850
the stairs?
楼梯的动作呢？

771
00:33:47.050 --> 00:33:50.930
Because I would, my business was to go up the stairs and get a box and bring it down or
因为我当时的工作就是上楼拿个箱子再拿下来，或者

772
00:33:50.930 --> 00:33:52.830
go up the stairs and put a box up on a shelf.
上楼把箱子放到架子上。

773
00:33:53.250 --> 00:33:54.950
I was like, what was I thinking?
我当时就在想，我到底在想什么啊？

774
00:33:55.250 --> 00:33:57.010
I couldn't move after.
之后我连动都动不了了。

775
00:33:57.070 --> 00:33:57.930
We've all done it.
我们都干过这种事。

776
00:33:57.930 --> 00:33:58.910
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

777
00:33:59.110 --> 00:33:59.390
We have.
确实干过。

778
00:33:59.470 --> 00:34:03.630
It was like the fourth day, I think it was, or the, it was the last day.
我想那是第四天，或者，那是最后一天。

779
00:34:03.770 --> 00:34:06.210
Was it the last day of shooting when I fell?
我摔倒的时候是拍摄的最后一天吗？

780
00:34:06.810 --> 00:34:07.930
I think it was.
我想是的。

781
00:34:08.110 --> 00:34:12.970
It was, thankfully, it was the last day of shooting because you didn't have to come back.
谢天谢地，那确实是拍摄的最后一天，因为你不用再回来了。

782
00:34:13.150 --> 00:34:14.450
You fell and hurt your knee.
你摔倒并伤到了膝盖。

783
00:34:14.550 --> 00:34:14.890
I did.
是的。

784
00:34:14.890 --> 00:34:15.690
Really badly.
伤得很重。

785
00:34:16.110 --> 00:34:18.150
Oh, and I didn't want anybody to know.
噢，我当时不想让任何人知道。

786
00:34:18.290 --> 00:34:19.870
I thought I was going to try and hide it.
我想试着把它藏起来。

787
00:34:20.030 --> 00:34:23.570
I was chasing Steve down court.
我当时在球场上追着史蒂夫跑。

788
00:34:24.290 --> 00:34:27.410
He went tearing after, and I went running after him.
他飞快地跑了出去，我也跟着追了过去。

789
00:34:27.410 --> 00:34:31.070
And my legs were just, like, not working.
然后我的腿就像是不听使唤了。

790
00:34:31.470 --> 00:34:32.930
They just stopped working.
它们突然就没法动了。

791
00:34:32.930 --> 00:34:36.450
And I just went flying, and I landed on my left knee.
我整个人直接飞了出去，左膝盖着地。

792
00:34:36.650 --> 00:34:37.630
On the concrete.
摔在水泥地上。

793
00:34:37.710 --> 00:34:38.870
Caught right on the concrete.
结结实实地磕在水泥地上。

794
00:34:39.210 --> 00:34:44.390
And I got up, and I kept running, and I kept playing, and then they said, cut.
我爬起来继续跑，继续演，然后他们喊了停。

795
00:34:44.530 --> 00:34:50.170
And I immediately went back to the back where I think there was a cooler filled with ice
我立刻退到后面，那里好像有个装满冰块

796
00:34:50.170 --> 00:34:51.530
and drinks or something like that.
和饮料之类的冷藏箱。

797
00:34:51.750 --> 00:34:56.810
And I just very quickly grabbed a Ziploc baggie and filled it with ice.
我很快抓起一个密封袋，往里面装满了冰块。

798
00:34:56.810 --> 00:34:58.230
And didn't say anything.
什么也没说。

799
00:34:58.390 --> 00:35:00.450
I just kind of sat there and sat down for a minute.
我就那样坐了一会儿。

800
00:35:00.930 --> 00:35:02.310
And it was really hurting.
当时真的疼得厉害。

801
00:35:02.550 --> 00:35:06.230
And so I just kind of quietly came out, and I sat down on the bench next to you.
于是我就悄悄地走出来，在你旁边的长椅上坐下了。

802
00:35:06.290 --> 00:35:07.950
And I had the ice pack on my knee.
当时我的膝盖上敷着冰袋。

803
00:35:08.310 --> 00:35:09.750
And I moved it for a second.
我把它挪开了一会儿。

804
00:35:09.850 --> 00:35:12.130
And you looked down at my knee, and you went, oh, my God!
你低头看了一眼我的膝盖，然后惊呼道：天哪！

805
00:35:12.190 --> 00:35:13.690
And I was like, shh.
我赶紧说：嘘。

806
00:35:14.110 --> 00:35:19.610
I was going to say, my memory is that that thing swelled up faSt.
我正想说，我的记忆里那东西肿得特别快。

807
00:35:19.990 --> 00:35:20.350
It was huge.
肿得好大。

808
00:35:20.510 --> 00:35:20.710
Yeah.
是啊。

809
00:35:21.150 --> 00:35:26.030
And I kind of remember being like, you got to—we got to get the medic.
我记得当时我说：你得——我们得去找医护人员。

810
00:35:26.230 --> 00:35:26.350
Yeah.
是啊。

811
00:35:26.350 --> 00:35:27.410
We got to tell somebody.
我们得告诉别人。

812
00:35:27.590 --> 00:35:27.670
Yeah.
是啊。

813
00:35:27.670 --> 00:35:28.510
Like, don't—
就像是，别——

814
00:35:28.510 --> 00:35:29.190
It didn't match.
看起来完全不对劲。

815
00:35:29.190 --> 00:35:29.550
Try to keep going.
试着继续拍。

816
00:35:29.810 --> 00:35:32.330
It didn't—my memory was it didn't match your other knee at all.
它没——我的记忆里它和你的另一条腿完全不一样。

817
00:35:32.410 --> 00:35:32.890
Not close.
差得远了。

818
00:35:33.330 --> 00:35:34.770
I was like, oh, my gosh.
我当时心想：天哪。

819
00:35:35.170 --> 00:35:35.220
Yeah.
是啊。

820
00:35:35.350 --> 00:35:37.230
And then, Jenna, I think you got the medic, didn't you?
然后，珍娜，我想是你去找的医护人员，对吧？

821
00:35:37.690 --> 00:35:43.650
You got the medic.
是你找来的医护人员。

822
00:35:43.650 --> 00:35:46.090
I'm like, I smell gas in the work bus.
我就像是在说：我闻到工作巴士里有煤气味。

823
00:35:46.150 --> 00:35:46.770
I know.
我知道。

824
00:35:47.070 --> 00:35:47.250
Yeah.
是啊。

825
00:35:47.430 --> 00:35:49.310
This entry needs attending to.
这事儿得处理一下。

826
00:35:49.330 --> 00:35:49.490
Yeah.
是啊。

827
00:35:49.690 --> 00:35:50.910
She was super sweet.
她人超级好。

828
00:35:51.010 --> 00:35:54.390
And she took one look, and she said, no, we're going to do an accident report.
她看了一眼就说：不行，我们得写一份事故报告。

829
00:35:54.490 --> 00:35:58.550
And I was sitting back in the back, and I was like, I am so mortified.
我当时坐在后面，心想：我真是太尴尬了。

830
00:35:58.550 --> 00:36:00.170
I didn't want to deal with this.
我不想处理这些麻烦事。

831
00:36:00.170 --> 00:36:00.790
It's fine.
没关系的。

832
00:36:00.790 --> 00:36:01.930
I'll be fine, blah, blah, blah.
我会没事的，诸如此类的。

833
00:36:01.970 --> 00:36:04.590
And she said, no, we're going to have you have that checked out.
但她说：不行，我们得让你去检查一下。

834
00:36:04.750 --> 00:36:07.210
And they filled out the forms and did the whole thing.
然后他们填了表格，走完了整个流程。

835
00:36:07.290 --> 00:36:10.170
And I was mortified because I was like, oh, my God.
我当时尴尬极了，心想：天哪。

836
00:36:10.170 --> 00:36:11.530
I'm not—we're not done filming.
我还没——我们还没拍完呢。

837
00:36:11.530 --> 00:36:17.270
And I'm—this is terrible, and blah, and I'd never hurt myself on a set before.
这太糟糕了，等等，我以前从没在片场受过伤。

838
00:36:17.570 --> 00:36:23.230
And this was my first three-day job ever, three days of filming.
而且这是我人生中第一份为期三天的拍摄工作。

839
00:36:23.430 --> 00:36:26.750
That was like the first—I had done two other jobs.
那是第一次——我之前只做过两份其他工作。

840
00:36:26.810 --> 00:36:27.570
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

841
00:36:27.570 --> 00:36:28.530
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

842
00:36:28.610 --> 00:36:28.670
It was huge.
确实非常重要。

843
00:36:29.430 --> 00:36:35.270
I remember you being worried, like, will they ever bring me back because I got hurt?
我记得你当时很担心，心想：我会不会因为受伤而被剧组弃用？

844
00:36:35.430 --> 00:36:38.590
And that's such a thing when you're an actor starting out.
当你刚入行做演员时，确实会有这种顾虑。

845
00:36:38.590 --> 00:36:44.770
Like, an accident happens, but you're afraid you'll get branded as difficult or, like, whatever.
比如，发生了意外，但你害怕被贴上“难搞”之类的标签。

846
00:36:45.030 --> 00:36:53.370
But that wasn't—that's—I mean, thankfully, I feel like, especially on The Office, that wasn't the tone of our set.
但那不是——那——我是说，谢天谢地，我觉得特别是在《办公室》剧组，我们的片场氛围并不是那样的。

847
00:36:53.590 --> 00:36:53.790
Yeah.
是啊。

848
00:36:53.890 --> 00:36:55.610
And you needed medical attention.
而且你需要医疗救助。

849
00:36:56.490 --> 00:36:58.450
And we did bring you back.
我们确实也让你回来了。

850
00:36:58.450 --> 00:36:58.730
Yeah.
是啊。

851
00:36:58.730 --> 00:36:58.930
Yeah.
是啊。

852
00:36:59.050 --> 00:36:59.750
It was all fine.
一切都很好。

853
00:36:59.810 --> 00:37:01.550
It was—I was so grateful.
那是——我当时非常感激。

854
00:37:01.550 --> 00:37:08.850
Well, you know, I want you to know that in the superfan version on Peacock, all of your stuff with Dwight—
嗯，你知道吗，我想让你知道，在Peacock平台的超级粉丝版里，你和德怀特的所有对手戏——

855
00:37:08.850 --> 00:37:13.710
imagine Dwight, like, it's like going down the court against each other is all in there.
想象一下德怀特，就像在球场上针锋相对一样，全都保留在里面了。

856
00:37:13.710 --> 00:37:14.530
In your face.
正面交锋。

857
00:37:14.610 --> 00:37:16.930
And clearly that happened before you hurt your knee.
显然那是发生在你膝盖受伤之前。

858
00:37:17.030 --> 00:37:17.150
Right.
没错。

859
00:37:17.150 --> 00:37:17.770
And you know what?
你知道吗？

860
00:37:17.810 --> 00:37:18.390
I'm so glad.
我真高兴。

861
00:37:18.570 --> 00:37:21.570
Now people will see how hard you were busting your ass on that court.
现在大家都能看到你在球场上有多拼命了。

862
00:37:21.690 --> 00:37:22.550
I was trying.
我当时确实很努力。

863
00:37:23.190 --> 00:37:23.430
Yeah.
是啊。

864
00:37:23.430 --> 00:37:28.170
I was—I was the—who was the guy who choreographed the basketball game?
我当时是——我是——那个负责编排篮球赛的人是谁来着？

865
00:37:28.290 --> 00:37:29.450
There was somebody there.
当时有个人在场。

866
00:37:29.450 --> 00:37:32.850
Oh, we had a stunt coordinator that choreographed the game.
哦，我们有个特技协调员负责编排那场比赛。

867
00:37:32.990 --> 00:37:38.990
But then there was parts of it that, you know, you guys were just running back and forth and kind of just freestyling.
但其中有些部分，你知道，你们只是在来回跑动，算是即兴发挥。

868
00:37:39.330 --> 00:37:44.250
But if you watch the superfan version, Madge and Dwight really square off a lot.
但如果你看超级粉丝版，玛奇和德怀特确实有很多正面交锋。

869
00:37:44.370 --> 00:37:45.150
What was that like?
那是什么感觉？

870
00:37:45.210 --> 00:37:46.150
Because we know rain.
因为我们了解雷恩。

871
00:37:46.390 --> 00:37:47.710
Rain goes all out.
雷恩总是全力以赴。

872
00:37:47.950 --> 00:37:48.070
Yeah.
是啊。

873
00:37:48.610 --> 00:37:57.410
There was a stunt coordinator who actually showed me how it was going to work, and it was like a choreographed thing.
有个特技协调员确实给我演示了该怎么做，那就像是编排好的动作。

874
00:37:57.530 --> 00:37:57.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

875
00:37:57.830 --> 00:38:00.990
And then when he grabs it from me, we're supposed to fight.
然后当他从我手里抢球时，我们本该打起来的。

876
00:38:01.010 --> 00:38:04.870
And there were a couple times where I think we even ended up on the ground.
有好几次我觉得我们甚至都打到地上了。

877
00:38:05.190 --> 00:38:05.570
Yeah.
是啊。

878
00:38:05.750 --> 00:38:05.930
Yeah.
没错。

879
00:38:06.010 --> 00:38:06.670
You did.
你们确实打到了。

880
00:38:06.810 --> 00:38:07.010
Yeah.
是啊。

881
00:38:07.370 --> 00:38:12.950
And then I was like, I'm not letting go of the ball.
当时我就想，我绝不松手。

882
00:38:13.030 --> 00:38:14.730
I'm not letting go of the ball.
我绝不松手。

883
00:38:14.890 --> 00:38:17.370
And he got into it, and I got into it.
他投入进去了，我也投入进去了。

884
00:38:17.430 --> 00:38:18.390
We started fighting.
我们开始打架了。

885
00:38:18.390 --> 00:38:23.710
And it was so much fun because he was like, I just got mad at him.
那真的很有趣，因为他当时——我对他真的生气了。

886
00:38:23.830 --> 00:38:25.030
I was like, back off, man.
我说，退后，伙计。

887
00:38:25.110 --> 00:38:25.930
Just back off.
退后点。

888
00:38:26.530 --> 00:38:28.630
And he goes, no, I'm not going to back off.
他说，不，我才不退后。

889
00:38:28.730 --> 00:38:30.730
And I'm going, get out of my face.
我说，离我远点。

890
00:38:30.850 --> 00:38:32.770
And I was like, in your face.
然后我说，正面交锋吧。

891
00:38:32.770 --> 00:38:36.050
It was really good and Phil's very honeSt.
那真的很棒，而且菲尔非常诚实。

892
00:38:36.050 --> 00:38:42.070
But that whole storyline between Dwight and Madge reminded me of like that, you know,
但德怀特和玛奇之间的那整条故事线让我想起了，你知道，

893
00:38:42.990 --> 00:38:48.950
eight-year-old boy on like the schoolyard that you're playing kickball with who goes so super hard.
就像操场上那个和你一起玩踢球游戏、拼命较真的八岁小男孩。

894
00:38:49.030 --> 00:38:49.150
Yeah.
是啊。

895
00:38:49.150 --> 00:38:52.470
And you're like, buddy, relax, except it's a grown man.
你会觉得，老兄，放松点，但这可是个成年男人。

896
00:38:52.670 --> 00:39:04.130
And if I hadn't hurt myself, we almost had this little secret thing that we were going to do behind the boxes when he takes a sip of water and he spills it all over his face.
如果我没受伤的话，我们本来有个小秘密，要在箱子后面演，就是他喝水时把水洒得满脸都是。

897
00:39:04.130 --> 00:39:04.410
Yeah.
是啊。

898
00:39:04.570 --> 00:39:12.110
Right before that, we were going to have this little secret thing behind the boxes, and that never came to fruition.
就在那之前，我们本来要在箱子后面演那个小秘密，但最终没能实现。

899
00:39:12.330 --> 00:39:13.010
What secret thing?
什么小秘密？

900
00:39:13.150 --> 00:39:13.930
Like Dwight and Madge hookup?
就像德怀特和玛奇要好上了？

901
00:39:13.930 --> 00:39:14.850
Like a little rope.
就像一根小绳子。

902
00:39:14.950 --> 00:39:17.510
Oh, like this was all foreplay on the court.
噢，就好像球场上的一切都只是前戏一样。

903
00:39:17.610 --> 00:39:18.610
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

904
00:39:18.610 --> 00:39:21.730
He met his physical match and he was turned on.
他遇到了旗鼓相当的对手，结果还兴奋起来了。

905
00:39:22.550 --> 00:39:27.670
We were going to come up with something, and then it never happened, unfortunately.
我们本来打算想出点什么，但遗憾的是，后来没成。

906
00:39:28.270 --> 00:39:32.630
But as it turned out, obviously, it never needed to happen.
但事实证明，显然，根本没必要发生。

907
00:39:32.970 --> 00:39:34.670
Well, I think it would have worked.
嗯，我觉得那本来是会奏效的。

908
00:39:34.770 --> 00:39:39.770
And you know what would have been great is if Angela found out and then really, like then Angela hated Madge.
你知道如果安吉拉发现了，然后真的开始讨厌玛奇，那该多棒啊。

909
00:39:39.810 --> 00:39:40.430
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

910
00:39:41.070 --> 00:39:46.990
Well, speaking of scenes in the warehouse where things were added, I want to jump to the boys and girls episode.
说到仓库里那些加戏的场景，我想跳到《男女员工》那一集。

911
00:39:46.990 --> 00:39:53.750
Because Dave Rogers wants you to know that he put an extra talking head of yours into boys and girls.
因为戴夫·罗杰斯想让你知道，他在《男女员工》里多加了一个你的采访镜头。

912
00:39:54.070 --> 00:40:00.510
This is when the documentary crew is filming down in the warehouse and they find Madge pushing a cart of supplies.
那是纪录片摄制组在仓库里拍摄时，发现玛奇在推着一车补给品。

913
00:40:00.850 --> 00:40:02.130
It's very funny.
非常搞笑。

914
00:40:02.390 --> 00:40:03.190
We're going to play it.
我们来放一下。

915
00:40:06.450 --> 00:40:08.610
I'm wanted in three states.
我在三个州被通缉。

916
00:40:12.530 --> 00:40:14.790
Did I say don't videotape me?
我没说别拍我吗？

917
00:40:14.790 --> 00:40:15.530
Don't tape me.
别拍我。

918
00:40:15.790 --> 00:40:16.130
Yeah.
是啊。

919
00:40:16.470 --> 00:40:18.470
I'm wanted in three states?
我在三个州被通缉？

920
00:40:18.470 --> 00:40:20.070
What is she wanted for?
她是因为什么被通缉的？

921
00:40:20.270 --> 00:40:21.270
Oh, my God.
天哪。

922
00:40:22.610 --> 00:40:23.730
That's hysterical.
太搞笑了。

923
00:40:23.930 --> 00:40:25.450
Do you even remember doing that?
你还记得当时拍那个吗？

924
00:40:25.590 --> 00:40:29.150
I feel like that must have been an improv moment.
我觉得那一定是即兴发挥的时刻。

925
00:40:29.330 --> 00:40:29.630
Totally.
绝对是。

926
00:40:29.930 --> 00:40:30.170
Right?
对吧？

927
00:40:30.470 --> 00:40:32.610
Or something they fed you on the day.
或者是当天他们让你说的台词。

928
00:40:33.330 --> 00:40:40.490
They were capturing little moments in the warehouse because right before that is Lonnie and they're filming him.
他们当时在捕捉仓库里的一些小瞬间，因为在那之前是朗尼，他们正在拍他。

929
00:40:40.750 --> 00:40:44.710
He's got that giant plastic like saran wrap and he's wrapping it around the boxes.
他拿着那种巨大的塑料保鲜膜，正把它缠在箱子上。

930
00:40:44.910 --> 00:40:47.670
And he's like, sometimes I pretend to be a car.
他说，有时候我假装自己是一辆车。

931
